5. BENEFICIARY REGISTRATION EXPERIENCE
This is one of the most important modules.
Design a clean, guided, multi-step registration process inspired by Workday's structured employee self-service forms.
Use a stepper or progress indicator.
Step 1: Employee Information
Fields:
Employee Number.
Full Name.
Department.
Email Address.
Where possible, automatically retrieve employee information from the existing employee data source.
Make retrieved employee information read-only where appropriate.
Step 2: Scheme Selection
Allow employees to select from available schemes.
Examples:
Pension Fund.
Provident Fund.
Insurance Beneficiary Scheme.
Death Benefit Scheme.
Only display active schemes retrieved from the backend.
Step 3: Beneficiary Information
Allow employees to add multiple beneficiaries dynamically.
Each beneficiary should have:
Full Name.
Relationship.
Date of Birth.
National ID / Passport Number.
Percentage Allocation.
Phone Number.
Physical Address.
Provide:
Add Beneficiary.
Remove Beneficiary.
Edit Beneficiary.
Show a clear allocation summary.
Example:
Total Allocation: 100%
Beneficiary A: 50%
Beneficiary B: 30%
Beneficiary C: 20%
Validation:
Allocation must equal exactly 100%.
No negative percentages.
Required fields must be completed.
Validate date formats.
Prevent invalid or incomplete submissions.
Display clear inline validation messages.
Step 4: Document Upload
Create a professional document upload interface.
Supported documents:
National ID.
Passport Copy.
Birth Certificate.
Marriage Certificate.
Other Supporting Documents.
Features:
Drag-and-drop upload.
Browse files.
Multiple file upload.
File name and size display.
Upload progress where supported.
Preview uploaded documents.
Download and remove documents where permitted.
Respect file types and size limits configured by the backend.
Step 5: Review and Submit
Display a comprehensive summary of:
Employee Information.
Selected Scheme.
Beneficiary Details.
Percentage Allocation.
Supporting Documents.
Provide:
Back.
Save Draft, if supported by existing backend.
Submit Nomination.
Show a confirmation dialog before final submission.
After successful submission, display a professional confirmation screen containing:
Success indicator.
Generated Reference Number.
Submission Date.
Current Status.
View Submission Details action.
The reference number must come from the backend. Never generate a fake reference number in the frontend.
